## Spring Cache Configuration with Redis

```java
@Configuration
@EnableCaching
public class CacheConfig {

    @Bean
    public RedisCacheManager cacheManager(RedisConnectionFactory connectionFactory) {
        // JSON serialization — human-readable, compatible across app restarts
        var objectMapper = new ObjectMapper()
            .registerModule(new JavaTimeModule())
            .activateDefaultTyping(
                BasicPolymorphicTypeValidator.builder().allowIfBaseType(Object.class).build(),
                ObjectMapper.DefaultTyping.NON_FINAL
            );

        var jsonSerializer = new GenericJackson2JsonRedisSerializer(objectMapper);

        var defaultConfig = RedisCacheConfiguration.defaultCacheConfig()
            .entryTtl(Duration.ofMinutes(10))       // default TTL: 10 minutes
            .serializeKeysWith(RedisSerializationContext.SerializationPair
                .fromSerializer(new StringRedisSerializer()))
            .serializeValuesWith(RedisSerializationContext.SerializationPair
                .fromSerializer(jsonSerializer))
            .disableCachingNullValues();             // don't cache null

        // Per-cache TTL overrides
        var cacheConfigs = Map.of(
            "users",    defaultConfig.entryTtl(Duration.ofHours(1)),
            "products", defaultConfig.entryTtl(Duration.ofMinutes(5)),
            "sessions", defaultConfig.entryTtl(Duration.ofDays(1))
        );

        return RedisCacheManager.builder(connectionFactory)
            .cacheDefaults(defaultConfig)
            .withInitialCacheConfigurations(cacheConfigs)
            .build();
    }
}
```

## Service Layer Caching

```java
@Service
public class UserService {

    private final UserRepository userRepository;

    // Cache result with key = userId parameter
    // Key stored as: users::42 (cacheName::key)
    @Cacheable(value = "users", key = "#userId")
    public UserDTO getUserById(Long userId) {
        // Only executes on cache miss
        return userRepository.findById(userId)
            .map(UserDTO::fromEntity)
            .orElseThrow(() -> new NotFoundException("User not found: " + userId));
    }

    // Cache multiple users by their IDs
    @Cacheable(value = "users", key = "#username.toLowerCase()")
    public UserDTO getUserByUsername(String username) {
        return userRepository.findByUsername(username)
            .map(UserDTO::fromEntity)
            .orElseThrow();
    }

    // Update entity AND update cache (write-through)
    @CachePut(value = "users", key = "#result.id")
    public UserDTO updateUser(Long userId, UpdateUserRequest request) {
        User user = userRepository.findById(userId).orElseThrow();
        user.setEmail(request.getEmail());
        return UserDTO.fromEntity(userRepository.save(user));
    }

    // Delete entity AND evict from cache
    @CacheEvict(value = "users", key = "#userId")
    public void deleteUser(Long userId) {
        userRepository.deleteById(userId);
    }

    // Clear entire cache (use sparingly — expensive!)
    @CacheEvict(value = "users", allEntries = true)
    public void clearUserCache() {
        log.info("Cleared all user cache entries");
    }

    // Conditional caching — only cache active users
    @Cacheable(value = "users", key = "#userId", condition = "#userId > 0",
               unless = "#result.status == 'DELETED'")
    public UserDTO getUserWithCondition(Long userId) {
        return userRepository.findById(userId).map(UserDTO::fromEntity).orElseThrow();
    }
}
```

## Cache Stampede Prevention

```java
// Problem: many requests hit DB simultaneously when a popular cache entry expires
// Solution: use a distributed lock or probabilistic early expiration

@Service
public class ProductService {

    private final StringRedisTemplate redisTemplate;
    private final ProductRepository productRepository;
    private static final String LOCK_PREFIX = "lock:product:";

    public ProductDTO getPopularProduct(Long productId) {
        String cacheKey = "product:" + productId;
        String cached = redisTemplate.opsForValue().get(cacheKey);
        if (cached != null) return deserialize(cached, ProductDTO.class);

        // Acquire lock — only one request rebuilds cache
        String lockKey = LOCK_PREFIX + productId;
        Boolean acquired = redisTemplate.opsForValue()
            .setIfAbsent(lockKey, "1", Duration.ofSeconds(5));

        if (Boolean.TRUE.equals(acquired)) {
            try {
                ProductDTO product = productRepository.findById(productId)
                    .map(ProductDTO::fromEntity).orElseThrow();
                redisTemplate.opsForValue().set(cacheKey, serialize(product), Duration.ofMinutes(10));
                return product;
            } finally {
                redisTemplate.delete(lockKey);
            }
        } else {
            // Another thread is rebuilding — wait briefly and retry
            Thread.sleep(100);
            return getPopularProduct(productId);
        }
    }
}
```

## Invalidation Strategies Summary

```
Strategy          | When Data is Stale      | Complexity | Data Loss Risk
TTL only          | Until TTL expires        | Low        | None
Explicit evict    | Until eviction fails/missed | Medium   | None
Write-through     | Never (always fresh)     | Medium     | None
Write-behind      | Brief async delay        | High       | Possible (crash)
Event-driven      | Until event processed    | High       | None
```

## Write-Through Pattern

```java
@Service
public class InventoryService {

    @CachePut(value = "inventory", key = "#productId")
    @Transactional
    public InventoryDTO updateStock(Long productId, int newQuantity) {
        // 1. Update DB
        Inventory inventory = inventoryRepository.findById(productId).orElseThrow();
        inventory.setQuantity(newQuantity);
        Inventory saved = inventoryRepository.save(inventory);

        // 2. @CachePut automatically updates cache with returned value
        return InventoryDTO.fromEntity(saved);
        // Cache is always in sync with DB — slightly higher write latency
    }
}
```

## Event-Driven Invalidation (Pub/Sub)

```java
// Publisher — user-service
@Service
public class UserCommandService {
    private final ApplicationEventPublisher eventPublisher;

    @Transactional
    public void updateUser(Long userId, UpdateUserRequest request) {
        User user = userRepository.findById(userId).orElseThrow();
        user.update(request);
        userRepository.save(user);

        // Publish domain event AFTER transaction commits
        eventPublisher.publishEvent(new UserUpdatedEvent(userId));
    }
}

// Cache invalidation listener
@Component
public class UserCacheInvalidator {
    private final CacheManager cacheManager;

    @EventListener
    @Async
    public void onUserUpdated(UserUpdatedEvent event) {
        Cache userCache = cacheManager.getCache("users");
        if (userCache != null) {
            userCache.evict(event.getUserId());
            log.debug("Evicted user cache for userId={}", event.getUserId());
        }
    }
}

// For cross-service cache invalidation via Kafka
@KafkaListener(topics = "user-events", groupId = "api-gateway-cache")
public void onUserEvent(UserEvent event) {
    if ("USER_UPDATED".equals(event.getType()) || "USER_DELETED".equals(event.getType())) {
        cacheManager.getCache("users").evict(event.getUserId());
    }
}
```

## Tag-Based Invalidation with Redis

```java
// Group related cache entries by tag — invalidate all at once
@Service
public class CategoryCacheService {

    private final StringRedisTemplate redis;

    // Store cache entry AND add key to tag set
    public void cacheWithTag(String tag, String key, Object value) {
        String tagSetKey = "cache_tag:" + tag;
        redis.opsForValue().set(key, serialize(value), Duration.ofHours(1));
        redis.opsForSet().add(tagSetKey, key);
        redis.expire(tagSetKey, Duration.ofHours(2));
    }

    // Invalidate all entries with this tag
    public void invalidateByTag(String tag) {
        String tagSetKey = "cache_tag:" + tag;
        Set<String> keysToDelete = redis.opsForSet().members(tagSetKey);
        if (keysToDelete != null && !keysToDelete.isEmpty()) {
            redis.delete(keysToDelete);
        }
        redis.delete(tagSetKey);
    }
}

// Usage: when a category changes, invalidate all cached products in that category
// invalidateByTag("category:electronics");
// → removes: product:101, product:202, product:303, listing:electronics
```

